                    {
                        "form_id": "b5ebed4d-11a2-45cf-bda5-7a8e84c19bf4",
                        "entry_id": "afa5c42a-d02e-320c-a5a1-02603e24cc58",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Mistkäfer"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                        "entry_id": "afa5c42a-d02e-320c-a5a1-02603e24cc58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "von Exkrementen lebender Käfer"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d406324b-21a4-487d-a572-8d5590357e69",
                                "sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                                "text": "„Mit Chepre (Skarabäus) gaben die Ägypter dem Mistkäfer einen Namen, der zwar auch nicht gerade Musik in ihren Ohren war, doch wenigstens in Gesellschaft ausgesprochen werden konnte.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6b55039-40da-4942-a878-56090b5210e2",
                                "sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                                "text": "„In den Augen der Ägypter ist dieser Mistkäfer ein richtiger Alchimist.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37f34396-a9aa-4b63-8ac8-f51e2f3ee0aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "afa5c42a-d02e-320c-a5a1-02603e24cc58",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: von Exkrementen lebender Käfer",
                        "target_lang_word": "dung beetle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dung beetle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                        "entry_id": "25c771c9-4016-3959-ac7c-69f65d0c2d20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the beetle of the family Scarabaeidae (scarab beetles), especially of the subfamilies Scarabaeinae and Aphodiinae, noted for rolling dung into balls for use as food or as brooding chambers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9a4378e-bbc3-4139-9409-223646540423",
                                                "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                                "text": "\"They went in together. His was accepted and mine rejected. The title of his paper was 'The Reproductive System of the Dung-Beetle'.\" There was a general laugh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e295f8b-a3be-4278-b5d2-2688bc6e5b38",
                                                "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                                "text": "What do dung beetles do? Adults and larvae of dung beetles feed only on dung and therefore are not a threat to the environment. This is in contrast to some other beetles found in dung pads, (not dung beetles) which feed on vegetable and other matter besides dung, while others are carnivorous. The activity of adult dung beetles can break up the dung pad, and most species bury the dung in the ground for feeding and breeding."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0d7542f-4ebc-46c9-a607-982e40dcd9e8",
                                                "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                                "text": "And then there are dung beetles, feces-eaters extraordinaire. The sacred dung scarab of Egypt symbolized resurrection and immortality, explaining why the ancient Egyptians often placed these beetles in tombs with the dead and why they painted dung beetle figures on their sarcophagi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf2e4d59-e308-4c93-9262-5fcebfe2fd8a",
                                                "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                                "text": "Some dung beetles, called rollers, use their back legs to roll dung into a smooth, tiny ball. […] The ancient Egyptians believed that the sun was rolled across the sky by a giant dung beetle named Khepri."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b03fa32-ef92-40a6-a4b2-e416efa9f93f",
                                                "sense_id": "77b452ef-1c53-318b-ad80-c9d001c810e9",
                                                "text": "Without dung beetles, the world would be a dirtier place. Animal dung can carry parasites and other germs that can make livestock sick. Farmers and ranchers need dung beetles to keep their pastures clean. Dung beetles clear away 80 percent of the cow manure in the whole of Texas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2850dc49-d70f-331c-8705-6f809b169fe1",
                                        "entry_id": "25c771c9-4016-3959-ac7c-69f65d0c2d20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the true dung beetles of subfamily Scarabaeinae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0f03f2b-84b3-41a0-a2aa-a5d75e6a51de",
                        "source_entry_id": "afa5c42a-d02e-320c-a5a1-02603e24cc58",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: von Exkrementen lebender Käfer",
                        "target_lang_word": "dor beetle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "faab4836-c1f3-41a1-82b5-00102b77bfd3",
                        "source_entry_id": "afa5c42a-d02e-320c-a5a1-02603e24cc58",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d6c2797-9e2d-3439-a946-c49c861b1106",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: von Exkrementen lebender Käfer",
                        "target_lang_word": "rola-bosta",
                        "target_lang_code": "pt",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rola-bosta",
                                "target_lang_code": "pt",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfe06aa8-4d6f-388b-a4d3-0292057460fe",
                                        "entry_id": "301508a1-9d91-30b2-8c0a-1bb60228a87c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nome comum a várias espécies de besouros (coleópteros da família dos escarabeídeos) robustos, em geral de cor escura (no Brasil há espécies de cores variadas, como verde-metálico), coprófagos - donde o seu nome: o adulto coloca seus ovos em bolas que prepara de esterco de mamíferos herbívoros, onde as larvas se desenvolvem e se alimentam"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Brazil",
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a0b86a9-0ce8-4068-a73a-ed54c78aa4e4",
                                                "sense_id": "bfe06aa8-4d6f-388b-a4d3-0292057460fe",
                                                "text": "“Os [besouros] rola-bosta são altamente sensíveis às mudanças ambientais, como alterações na temperatura, umidade, vegetação e estrutura do habitat.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
